  "lead_raw_text": " This structure of Na2S2O2 (NaS2O) crystallizes in triclinic symmetry with space group P1 and a 12-atom unit cell containing Na4S4O4. The 12 independent Wyckoff orbits correspond to seven elements, with Na, S, and O each represented by two crystallographically distinct orbits. Geometry-derived coordination analysis identifies tetrahedral environments for two S and two O centers, each with four Na neighbors, while Na centers show five- and six-neighbor environments. The geometric neighbor graph forms a single three-dimensional component spanning all 12 sites. Validated polyhedron-sharing analysis shows corner- and edge-sharing between tetrahedral S and O polyhedra, and edge-sharing between six-vertex Na and tetrahedral S polyhedra.\n<CRYSTAL_START>",
